# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
*.binlog

# ── Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── .NET / MAUI intermediates ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No blanket *.dll / *.pdb / *.ttf rule here: bin/ and obj/ already cover build output, and a
# blanket binary rule silently drops committed assets — the Gallery's OpenSans fonts, for one.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.app/
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.msix
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
project.lock.json
project.assets.json
*.nuget.dgspec.json

# The generated Android/iOS resource designers are build output, not source.
**/Resources/Resource.designer.cs

# ── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Local-only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a real key. The pipeline reads its three secrets from Azure DevOps
# pipeline variables (Github.PAT, AzureDevOps.PAT, NuGetApiKey), not from a file.
*.snk
*.pfx
secrets.json
appsettings.Local.json
